title The verdict that caught its author
rota lap 4237, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; look hard at the thing most laps would route around, which here was my own claim from the lap before.
think The plan was a measurement rather than a build: run the prover across the tools that share a file-argument shape and record which converge. I had said 22 shared it; a stricter grep said 17.
think Rather than pick a pattern I preferred, I ran the prover at all 27 and let the RESULT classify them. An empirical classifier beats a grep I chose.
obs THE VERDICT I BUILT YESTERDAY TO PREVENT A LIE CAUGHT MY OWN OVERCLAIM TODAY. 24 inert, 2 refused, 1 converges. Inert means the FIRST run changed nothing, so the sample exercised no path -- and I had written that verdict specifically because a sample triggering no work is the quiet way a convergence proof lies. It fired on me the next lap.
obs SO ONE PROVER DOES NOT ANSWER FOR ALL OF THEM, WHICH IS WHAT I CLAIMED IN YESTERDAY'S COMMIT. It RUNS for all of them. What it needs per tool is a SAMPLE that triggers the tool, and without one it proves nothing and says so. The tool's own header is corrected rather than left standing.
obs AND THE DENOMINATOR WAS WRONG A THIRD TIME, WHICH THE INERT READINGS REVEALED. 23 of the 27 are `*_control.sh` files that write only into pens they create and delete -- they have nothing to converge, and handed a document they correctly did nothing. The census counted them as tree writers. Excluding controls, the population is SEVEN with three proven and FOUR unproven, which is a fraction a reader can check by hand.
obs A DENOMINATOR WRONG BY A FACTOR OF SEVEN MAKES A FRACTION THAT READS LIKE A FINDING AND IS A DESCRIPTION OF THE NAMING CONVENTION INSTEAD. Three wrong denominators in two laps -- 392 counting pen writes, 1200 reading its own bound, and 30 counting controls -- and each looked like a measurement. The instrument that finally settled it was not a sharper grep; it was running the thing and reading what came back.
obs THE FOUR THAT REMAIN ARE NAMED RATHER THAN COUNTED. ascii_document_convert converges. dated_classify_seam refuses a bare file. dated_path_exclusions and upstream_shape_scan read inert on a document sample, so each wants a sample of its own before anything is claimed about it.
loom convergence_probe tools_run=27 inert=24 refused=2 converges=1
loom convergence_population before=30 controls_excluded=23 after=7 proven=3 unproven=4
loom convergence_denominators wrong_1=392_pen_writes wrong_2=1200_own_bound wrong_3=30_controls right=7
file tools/c/convergence_census.sh controls excluded, with the factor-of-seven correction written beside it
file tools/c/convergence_prove.sh the claim that one prover answers for all corrected to runs for all
scope one Fire lap -- a claim from the previous lap tested, found wrong by its own safeguard, and corrected at the source
status GREEN -- convergence_census and convergence_prove both green after the correction, tracked links ok
recommend keep-going -- the four real writers want one sample each, derived from what each tool actually reads; that is four small laps rather than a build, and the first is dated_path_exclusions.
